  "dom_id": "step-q53664",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245089/assets/01b6ade0a9b4945c0381848092e9b2289f823c49b2c5c138a29187e7f541787c.png)\n\nThe two pentagons shown above are similar. What is the correct similarity statement?",
  "worked_solution": "Since, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠A≅∠U,\\,∠B≅∠V,\\,∠C≅∠W,\\,∠D≅∠X,\\,∠E≅∠Y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n- $A$ corresponds to $U,$\n\n- $B$ corresponds to $V,$\n\n- $C$ corresponds to $W,$\n\n- $D$ corresponds to $X,$\n\n- $E$ corresponds to $Y.$\n\nTherefore, $ABCDE∼UVWXY.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
